e hands the room over to her we  know this is a real passing of the torch  when she walks out there's so much  history that pours in it's a bittersweet  end for someone who really did give her  whole life to the space program we had  seen that the intelligence services  managed to get sergey and his family out  of the ussr in a video call and know  that for all her efforts she won't be  able to outrun the consequences of her  mistakes she goes back to her office and  plays the piano and we cut to happy  valley getting ready to strap kelly to  the top of the m sam we see that she's  wearing a modified version of alexey's  suit there's a last minute exchange of i  love use between her and ed and then  there's just an absolutely perfect bit  of television it looks amazing the music  puts you right there with her and even  though i never feared that they might  kill kelly and her unborn child the  satisfaction of her knowing she's going  to make it when you see her smile as she  approaches the phoenix is short-lived  because ed still has to manage a  ballistic descent i must have watched  this 10 times now and from the moment  she separates to the smile stretching  across her face to ed's relief knowing  that no matter what happens next he got  his daughter to safety it gets me every  single time there's no time even to  process that though because karen is  outside of jsc and when she tries to  call jimmy's phone she notices that his  friends have it she'll find him tied up  in the back of the van and see that it's  filled with explosives when the  terrorist sees her he detonates the bomb  remotely and it destroys the building  and kills her jimmy survives to find her  in her last moments inside mission  command we see molly helping survivors  get out later we'll learn that she will  also lose her life while she's doing  that elada goes looking for margot and  finds that half of her office was  sheared off in the blast as the camera  pulls out to show the devastation w