 a  year to survive and to start the first  colony on the red planet that's the kind  of thing that this show does that i keep  coming back for this had some amazing  moments like you'd expect but i like  this finale slightly less than season  2's for a couple of reasons the show has  a way of introducing things that can  feel insignificant at the moment but  then circle back around and deliver a  big payoff i mean most of the latest  story in the first season felt like an  interesting but unconnected side story  and now it all makes a lot of sense  season 3 still had a lot of that going  on i think ed's story is the best  example i saw grown men crying in the  comments because their favorite space  program avatar wasn't the first person  to land on mars but i think that only  added to the ending which was about him  redeeming himself as a father sure not  being first on the moon is something  that's haunted him but as we learned  when he was buried in the hab so was the  way he left things with shane before he  died for him to be there and be  essential in kelly making it to safety  on the phoenix and to know that he was  okay with sacrificing himself if it came  to that makes him come out of this  season as even more of a boss and he got  to do what he does best and live to tell  the story margot and elena also had a  fantastic season even though it was hard  to watch at times there are obvious  parallels to her mentor von braun but we  understand her character much better and  can see how she ended up where she did  while knowing that her intentions were  mostly pure she put everything she had  into making space exploration what it is  in this timeline and that little bit of  her human nature she indulged in falling  in love led to places she couldn't come  back from elena will be a great  replacement though and it was fitting to  have her final act in the usb getting  sergey and his family to safety  karen and molly's deaths hit  unbelievably hard although molly's was  almost a blink and you'd miss it  situation the way the camera lingered on  the man she saved watching her walk back  into the smoke stood out but if i hadn't  paused to look at the paper i might not  have put things together in my first  watch when i finished i honestly  wondered how many people might miss that  karen's death felt like a complete shock  which i guess was the point and i  suppose if you think about it her arc  was complete when you have a show that  moves so quickly through time it makes  sense to deliver these dramatic endings  rather than have these great characters  just sort of fade away but one minute  she was about to step into the ceo role  at helios and the next she's just gone  both of the actors here gave great  performances they brought these  characters to life in a way that they're  both really memorable and they're gonna  be missed and geez my thoughts are  really just with wayne after the way  this played out i loved how they came  together and how molly gave her the i'm  a selfish prick speech that added to her  hero's ending and aligned her with the  show's thesis yeah she has been a prick  at times and that's been fantastic to  watch but she's also been selfless when  she needed to be and that's what she's  doing in her final moments i've been  critical of both jimmy and danny's  stories this season so i don't want to  beat a dead horse but in case you  haven't been following along in my  opinion these were the weakest elements  of this season they did manage to make  danny's situation more sympathetic but  only after they exhausted me with the  whole thing his bad behavior did add a  lot of tension along the way but i  mostly just wanted him to go away for it  rather than wanting to see him come back  around and redeem himself the banishing  seems like a fitting ending for how  things played out but it's a temporary  one that feels a little dangling since  we know that it'll be in the past by the  time the next season starts and i do  want to mention that even though i  didn't like a lot of what they gave him  to do casey w johnson did a great job in  the hab and in that last moment where he  comes to ed to salvage something with  his performance it's a little bit worse  with jimmy because i'm not even sure how  we're supposed to feel about that he  didn't know what his friends were up to  and you can see how he was sucked in but  what happens next is he the lone  survivor do they try to pin it on him or  does the fact that he has hero parents  and that he was a victim in all this  mean that nothing happens to him that he  just turns things around and that's what  we're going to be seeing next time i  honestly don't know and this is a part  of the bigger problem i had with this  ending i like the hope and i like that  space exploration will continue because  of this series of unexpected events to  bring things full circle there's the  parallel of ellen saying maybe the  republican party needs some destroying  and the fact that jsc is literally  destroyed in an attack that has a lot of  similarities to the oklahoma city  bombing in our timeline sometimes it's  in the reaction after a crisis or  catastrophe where change can happen but  there are a lot of things left up in the  air so it doesn't feel as neat it  doesn't have that feeling of everything  falling into place that you got at the  end of season two and to be fair that's  a pretty high bar so by no means am i  saying that this wasn't enjoyable or  that it was bad the highs were  absolutely high and that's enough to  keep me coming back when it's doing what  it does best there really isn't anything  else like it on tv i guess we'll have to  wait and see how they handle the  transition to know if it'll make sense i  had been worried about the lack of  likable new characters and i do think  that kelly and will certainly are a good  starting point for season four deb ended  up having a pretty satisfying arc by the  end of the season and with karen out of  the way i'm sure we're gonna see more of  him everyone else is getting old a  little too old and that makes it feel a  little slim but hey with margot in  moscow we'll finally get to see things  from the soviet perspective which is  something that's been lacking in this  show and we'll get a ton of new  characters there it is something to look  forward to and i think that's a great  place to leave things  let me know in the comments what you  thought about season three overall what  you thought about the finale and what  you're hoping to see in season four  please like this video if you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already and thanks for watching  i'll talk to you soon

